scope: Join code migration + rotate, taskboard 411. Nancy re-reviewed e25878a25 directly via 'git show' after her earlier PROCEED was CONDITIONAL on two items; both now confirmed closed in her words: Item 1 (stale comment) CONFIRMED FIXED - 'The correction now lives at the same location as the error it corrects, which was the actual defect I raised; a fix elsewhere in the file was not sufficient and now isn't the situation.' Item 2 (rotate silently gating an open event) CONFIRMED FIXED - she verified all three prompt branches and that 'The write path is unchanged and still atomic ... the three-way branch only selects dialog copy; every branch that reaches confirm() and gets accepted performs the identical, correct write', so concern 1's atomicity/fail-closed property is untouched. She endorsed the new tests asserting prompt TEXT: 'That's the right thing to assert, since the warning text is the actual behavior under review here, not an implementation detail.' On my direct question she ruled AGAINST moving the state read inside the transaction: Firestore transactions retry on contention, so confirm() could fire repeatedly for one click - 'a worse defect than the one being traded away'. She named one residual she explicitly declined to fix: a second admin writing a different code between the read and the confirm click would be silently overwritten by the accepted rotation - 'not a correctness bug ... last-write-wins on a single mutable document, ordinary for this kind of admin tool, and trivially recoverable'. Her closing: 'No other findings against this diff.' HER EARLIER PASSES in this sequence were: PAUSE on the first submission (COPY not atomic; no rotate path anywhere) - both real, both fixed in 208d34a1c. This record covers the CONSOLE migration only: it does NOT cover running COPY or PURGE against production data, which is an operator click.
